SEG = "FLD"
CAT = "fvicField"
Q = [
    ("You come to a farm fence while hunting. The booklet's first advice is:",
     "If there is a gate, use it", ["Climb over at a post", "Crawl under the wire", "Jump it with the rifle slung"],
     "The booklet says if there is a gate, use it, and never climb a fence while carrying a firearm."),
    ("Why does the booklet warn about crossing electric fences with a firearm?",
     "A shock can clench your hands", ["The wire can bend the barrel", "The current can fire a primer", "The wire can scratch the stock"],
     "The booklet says an electric shock can make your muscles contract and your hands clench, so unload and open the action before you get near an electric fence."),
    ("The booklet says to pay attention when walking along riverbeds and dry creek-beds with a firearm because they are often:",
     "Slippery or icy", ["Full of snakes", "Private property", "Too noisy for game"],
     "The booklet's hazards section says riverbeds and dry creek-beds are often slippery or icy, so take care to keep control of the muzzle."),
    ("You stumble while carrying your rifle. The booklet says your first and most important responsibility is to:",
     "Keep the muzzle safe", ["Protect the telescopic sight", "Hold on to the sling", "Break the fall with the stock"],
     "The booklet says if you fall or stumble, your first responsibility is to keep the muzzle pointed safely and not touch the trigger."),
    ("For hunters who travel to remote areas, the instructors manual says to consider carrying:",
     "An EPIRB", ["A spare rifle", "A second spotlight", "Extra decoys"],
     "The manual's personal safety points list a mobile phone, first aid kit, compass or GPS, torch and wet weather gear, and say an EPIRB should be considered, especially in remote areas."),
    ("It is raining heavily. To keep water out of the barrel, the booklet says to carry the firearm with the muzzle:",
     "Down, clear of the ground", ["Pointed up at the sky", "Plugged with a cloth", "Held level out ahead"],
     "The booklet says to keep the muzzle pointed down in heavy rain or snow without letting it touch the ground, and never push a plug of cloth into the barrel."),
    ("To keep snow and mud out of a barrel, the booklet suggests:",
     "Tape over the muzzle", ["A cloth plug in the bore", "A cork in the chamber", "A plastic bag over the action"],
     "The booklet suggests a small square of insulation or masking tape over the muzzle, and warns never to insert a plug of cloth or other material into the barrel."),
    ("Your firearm misfires. The booklet says you must check the barrel from:",
     "The breech end", ["The muzzle end", "Either end at random", "The side ejection port only"],
     "The booklet says after a misfire you must check the barrel, from the breech end, in case a bullet is stuck in it."),
    ("Moving through heavy scrub with an exposed-hammer firearm, the booklet warns the hammer may:",
     "Get cocked by the scrub", ["Rust in the damp air", "Fall off the action", "Lock the trigger solid"],
     "The booklet says watch for twigs getting into the barrel in heavy scrub, and with an exposed hammer, take care it is not cocked accidentally by brushing through scrub."),
    ("With a firearm in hand, the booklet says to cross a stream by:",
     "Walking through the water", ["Jumping across on rocks", "Wading with the gun loaded", "Throwing the gun across first"],
     "The booklet's safety guides say to walk through a stream while carrying firearms rather than jumping or crossing on rocks, which are often slippery."),
    ("In the booklet's 'semi-ready' state for a bolt action rifle, the rifle is held in both hands with:",
     "A round partly chambered", ["The bolt fully closed and cocked", "The magazine removed", "The safety catch off"],
     "The booklet describes semi-readiness as holding the firearm in both hands with a cartridge pushed partly forward into the chamber, closing the action only once the target is identified and the shot is safe."),
    ("A break-open shotgun is semi-ready, according to the booklet, when carried:",
     "Open, with shells loaded", ["Closed with the safety on", "Closed with the hammer down", "Empty with shells in hand"],
     "The booklet says a break-open shotgun can be carried in the hinged open position with cartridges in the chambers; it is safe while open and can be closed and fired quickly."),
    ("When spotlighting vermin from a vehicle, the booklet says how many firearms should be in use at once?",
     "One", ["Two", "Three", "One per window"],
     "The booklet's spotlighting rules say never have more than one firearm in use at any one time."),
    ("Where does the booklet say the shooter should sit when spotlighting from a vehicle?",
     "The front passenger seat", ["On the tray of the ute", "In the back seat", "On the bonnet"],
     "The booklet says to position the shooter in the front passenger seat, firearm unloaded and pointing out the front passenger window, and never to shoot from the back seat."),
    ("After shooting an animal while spotlighting, the booklet says the shooter should:",
     "Unload, then get out", ["Get out, then unload", "Pass the rifle to the driver", "Leave it loaded on the seat"],
     "The booklet says the shooter should unload the firearm and exit the vehicle before placing the firearm on the ground."),
    ("The booklet says spotlighting must not be done:",
     "On public roads", ["On your own farm", "With a licensed driver", "After midnight"],
     "The booklet says you must not spotlight on public roads or in recognised deer habitat, and refers to the Game Management Authority for details."),
    ("The booklet calls riding in the back of a ute or a roofless 'bush basher' while hunting:",
     "Plainly irresponsible", ["Fine on private land", "Safe at low speeds", "Allowed with a helmet"],
     "The booklet says riding in the back of a utility, tray vehicle or bush basher is plainly irresponsible and extremely dangerous, and urges everyone to wear a seat belt."),
    ("Before shooting anywhere, the booklet says you need:",
     "The landowner's say-so", ["A council noise permit", "A hunting club escort", "A spotter with you"],
     "The booklet's section on where and when you may use firearms says the permission of the land owner is required before shooting anywhere."),
    ("The booklet says a good first step to avoid alarming neighbours when you shoot is to:",
     "Let them know your plans", ["Shoot only at night", "Use a suppressor", "Fire in short bursts"],
     "The booklet says take steps so your shooting does not endanger, frighten or annoy neighbours, and telling them what you are doing is always a good first step."),
    ("Which firearm does the booklet say is the only one suitable for shooting birds on the wing?",
     "A shotgun", ["A .22 rimfire", "A centre fire rifle", "An air rifle"],
     "The booklet says a shotgun is the only firearm suitable for birds on the wing, because a rifle fired into the air can strike someone when the bullet falls back to earth."),
    ("Under Victoria's game rules quoted in the booklet, what must duck hunters not use or carry in the hunting area?",
     "Toxic shot", ["Steel shot", "Plastic decoys", "Chest waders"],
     "The booklet says duck hunters cannot use or possess toxic shot in Victoria while out in the hunting area, and points to the Game Management Authority for non-toxic shot sizes."),
    ("Which body issues Game Licences and manages open and closed seasons in Victoria?",
     "The Game Management Authority", ["Victoria Police Licensing Division", "Parks Victoria rangers", "The Firearms Appeals Committee"],
     "The booklet says the Game Management Authority is an independent statutory authority that issues Game Licences, manages seasons, enforces game hunting laws and educates hunters."),
    ("A 15-year-old junior licence holder wants to hunt duck. The booklet says they need:",
     "Their own Game Licence", ["Only the adult's Game Licence", "No Game Licence at all", "A category C licence"],
     "The booklet says anyone hunting game in Victoria, including juniors aged 12 to 17, must hold a current Game Licence endorsed for the game they hunt."),
    ("Before even a short local hunting trip, the instructors manual says you should:",
     "Tell someone your plans", ["Clean your rifle twice", "Buy fresh ammunition", "Call the local police station"],
     "The manual says to tell somebody where you are going and when you expect to return, even if it is only a short trip locally."),
]
